\section{Discussion}
\label{sec:discussion}

The Symbolic Mirage manifests through two channels: correlated constraints compress $K_{\text{eff}} < 2$ (\emph{direct}), while answer-coupled constraints collapse MAX-SAT to vote counting (\emph{indirect}; Eq.~\ref{eq:degenerate}). The bias ratio gradient ($4.97\times$ Mistral $> 3.93\times$ Qwen $> 2.88\times$ LLaMA) confirms this scales with capability; thinking-mode degeneration ($\kappa = 0.91$, Qwen3) marks the upper bound. The independence-accuracy trade-off instantiates the classic ensemble tension \citep{krogh1994neural, brown2005diversity}. If traces do not reflect actual reasoning \citep{turpin2024language}, the mirage is inherent to extraction. An alternative $\sigma(c, a)$ via Z3 semantic evaluation could in principle avoid degeneration (Eq.~\ref{eq:degenerate}), but faces circular dependency and converges at $\text{BR} = 4.97\times$.

